Interactive USD edits of the points of meshes sharing their points, subdivided, instanced or large

Two meshes are given the same points array, so they use one USD buffer (and the render delegate makes the second a
duplicate of the first); a subdivided mesh, the prototype of a point instancer and a mesh of 65536 points also get
their points edited. The steps:
- the points of one of the shared meshes changed, then the other given the same new points;
- one of the shared meshes removed while the other still uses the points, then the points of the other changed;
- the subdivided mesh's points moved, then its subdivision turned off and its points moved in the same edit;
- the points of the instancer's prototype changed;
- the subdivided mesh replaced by a large grid, whose points are then moved.
The stage is re-rendered after each edit, and each render must show the new positions and nothing at the old ones.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session,
and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. The legacy reader doesn't delete removed prims, a known issue reported as a
warning: the "usd" pass has its own reference image (ref/reference.usd.tif), where the removed mesh is still there and the
prototype itself is rendered between the instances.

author: Cyril Pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
